## Why This Is Asked
Tests for per-user feature flags are common in SaaS apps. This question checks the ability to seed data, perform API-driven state changes, and verify UI behavior across login and page reloads in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Per-user feature flags and API seed/reset
- End-to-end UI verification of dynamic layouts
- Test isolation and deterministic CI runs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example using Playwright-like syntax (pseudocode)
// seedUser(), setFlag(), login() are helper utilities
test('compact dashboard toggling', async ({ page, request }) => {
  const { userId, email, password } = await seedUser(request);
  await setFlag(request, userId, 'CompactDashboard', true);
  await login(page, email, password);
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-compact')).toBeVisible();
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-compact')).toBeVisible();
  await setFlag(request, userId, 'CompactDashboard', false);
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-full')).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you guard against flaky UI assertions caused by caching?
- How would you extend the test to cover multiple user segments (roles/regions) and parallel execution?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes a beginner-friendly yet realistic E2E scenario: draft persistence, UI interactions, and end-to-end verification across multiple pages (feed and profile), with API mocking and test data isolation.

## Key Concepts

- LocalStorage persistence and autosave behavior
- End-to-end API mocking with intercept/stub
- Test data seeding and isolation
- Cross-page assertions and state verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Cypress example
describe('Drafts and Publish', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    // Seed test user
    cy.request('POST', '/api/test/setup', { user: 'test-user' }).then(() => {
      // Mock the publish API
      cy.intercept('POST', '/api/posts', {
        statusCode: 201,
        body: { id: '123', status: 'published' }
      }).as('publishPost');
    });
    cy.visit('/compose');
  });

  it('autosaves draft, preserves on reload, and publishes to feed and profile', () => {
    // Compose a draft
    cy.get('.rich-text-editor').type('My new post draft');

    // Wait for autosave (15 seconds)
    cy.wait(15000);
    cy.window().then(win => {
      expect(win.localStorage.getItem('draft')).to.exist;
    });

    // Reload and verify draft restoration
    cy.reload();
    cy.get('.rich-text-editor').should('contain', 'My new post draft');

    // Publish the post
    cy.get('[data-testid="publish-btn"]').click();
    cy.wait('@publishPost');

    // Verify draft is cleared
    cy.window().then(win => {
      expect(win.localStorage.getItem('draft')).to.be.null;
    });

    // Verify post appears in main feed
    cy.visit('/feed');
    cy.contains('My new post draft').should('be.visible');

    // Verify post appears on profile
    cy.visit('/profile/test-user');
    cy.contains('My new post draft').should('be.visible');
  });
});
```

